 problematic because  i already did that right here but that  likely means 1500 calories at least is  being used as a maintenance calorie  level and i don't know 500 calories  actually seems pretty low for  maintenance considering her activity  level even outside of this journey never  mind a goal to gain muscle so i do  wonder if there was maybe some severe  metabolic damage from her bikini model  days when she was apparently consuming a  thousand calories a day that maybe she  hasn't taken the time to properly  reverse diet out of regardless of where  or how things have netted out chelsea  and i agree that you know it's very  difficult to actively build muscle  without some amount of a caloric surplus  and if 1500 calories is her surplus well  it's not the journey that i would be  investing in at the moment so if we were  to look to add just the minimum amount  of carbs and fats that we just discussed  we would be looking at closer to  1925 calories which still actually seems  quite modest to me but it's a far more  appropriate starting place for sure now  i'm admittedly filming this well in  advance so i'm really not sure how  things have netted out at this point but  in her january 30th blog post and her  february first blog post she discusses  slightly upping her fats and calories so  i am glad to see her tweaking her diet  based on how her body responds and feels  each week i expect she's also going to  need to up her carbs a lot more as well  which i know may be a more psychological  challenge for her given her diet history  and also maybe what she's become  accustomed to much of cassie's instagram  feed has featured low or lower carb  meals she also kicked off her last 90  day journey doing legit keto and i  suspect that in her fitness competition  days she cut carbs pretty low too so i  get that old habits die hard  it's often so deeply ingrained in a lot  of our heads that protein is for muscle  and carbs promote fat gain but that is  scientifically untrue